  "source": "Swedish Alcohol Retail Monopoly",
  "note": [
    "Indicator definition: Proportion (%) of persons below the age of 25 who were asked for ID in Systembolaget's stores during test purchases of alcoholic beverages.Systembolaget appoints an independent company to conduct regular test purchases in the stores. The test purchases are conducted by persons in the age group 20–24 years and between 5,500 and 6,000 test purchases are conducted per year. The method was revised in 2007 and comparisons of data before and after 2007 should therefore be interpreted with caution."
  ]
